# N3 example: now-and-language-builtins.
# Companion to now-and-language-builtins.eye/.srl: N3 has no builtin to
# extract a literal's language tag, so (matching the .srl companion's own
# `STRLANG`/`sameTerm` check) this confirms the language-tagged text by
# comparing it against a French-tagged copy of the same string via
# `log:equalTo`, rather than introspecting the tag directly. The datetime
# is encoded as a plain RDF list of its components (there is no dedicated
# datetime term the way Eyelang's `datetime(...)` compound is), matched
# structurally to pull out the year.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix : <http://example/>.

:msg :text "bonjour"@fr.
:clock :event (2026 5 15 10 20 30).

{?msg :text ?text. ?text log:equalTo "bonjour"@fr} => {?msg :sameLanguageAs true}.
{?event :event (?year ?month ?day ?hour ?minute ?second)} => {?event :eventYear ?year}.
